## Comments
[2026-09-08T04:11:07Z] Norman Nunley, Jr: Closed as by-design for the second half: 'key: ' with a trailing space for an empty comment text or an empty first description line is the intended encoding — the grammar's value is possibly-empty after '<key>: ', so a consumer splitting on the first ': ' gets an empty string either way, and emitting a bare 'key:' would need a second parse rule for no gain. Pinned by tests in tests/test_porcelain.sh (6d81359). The first half (leading prose in a legacy comments section) is fixed in the same commit.
